dict(id="MJF-011", title="CV tailoring with mandatory factual containment validation",
     area="ai", priority="critical", complexity="L", milestone=M_CV,
     problem="Tailoring is the highest-value AI feature and the highest-risk: an LLM asked to improve a CV for a job will invent experience unless actively prevented.",
     business="A fabricated line on a CV is a lie told in the candidate's name to an employer. It can cost them the role and their reputation. This is the product's most serious safety requirement.",
     technical="Generate a tailored version constrained to the parsed CV as the sole factual source, then run a post-generation validator that diffs against the source and rejects any new employer, title, date, certification or skill.",
     solution="Implement the containment validator as a hard gate, independent of the prompt. Prompt compliance is necessary but insufficient, and a job description can carry an injection requesting exactly the fabrication we forbid. On rejection, retry once with a stricter prompt, then report that tailoring could not be completed safely. Persist containment_passed; the schema already requires it to be non-null for a tailored version.",
     acceptance=["Output introducing any employer, title, date, certification or skill absent from the source is rejected",
                 "Unvalidated output is never surfaced to the candidate or attached to an application",
                 "The candidate sees a diff against the source before the tailored CV is used",
                 "containment_passed is recorded on every tailored version",
                 "A prompt-injection attempt in the job description cannot defeat the validator"],
     deps=["MJF-005", "MJF-009"], testing="Adversarial suite: job descriptions demanding skills the candidate lacks; descriptions containing explicit injection instructions; a mocked provider returning fabricated content, asserting rejection. This suite is a release gate."),

